    "title": "Kansas seniors: Get $50 for fresh produce - NewsBreak",
    "text": "TOPEKA, Kan. (KSNW) — Starting July 14, eligible seniors in Kansas can get $50 in coupons to use at local farmers markets. The coupons can be used to buy fresh fruits, vegetables, herbs, and Kansas-grown honey. The program is designed to help older adults eat healthy while also supporting local farmers. To qualify, you must be at least 60 years old—or 55 if you’re a member of an Indian Tribal Organization—and meet income guidelines. Applications are open until Sept. 30, but supplies are limited, so seniors are encouraged to apply early . Participating vendors at farmers’ markets will have signs showing they accept the coupons. More details, including how to apply and where to use the coupons, are available on the Kansas Senior Farmers Market Nutrition Program website . For more Kansas news, click here . Keep up with the latest breaking news by downloading our mobile app and signing up for our news email alerts . Sign up for our Storm Track 3 Weather app by clicking here . To watch our shows live on our website, click here. For the latest news, weather, sports, and streaming video, head to KSN-TV.",
